## What does not go with what, and why.
compatibility-material-names-steel = steel
compatibility-material-names-aluminium = aluminium
compatibility-material-names-iron = cast iron
compatibility-material-names-glass = glass
compatibility-material-names-copper = copper
compatibility-material-names-brass = brass
compatibility-can-heat-reason = { $name } does not heat a { $m } vessel: it needs a magnetic metal (cast iron, magnetic steel). The hob simply does not «see» it.
compatibility-can-heat-reason-2 = { $name } has a round bottom: on a hob it touches it at a single point and hardly heats up. Such vessels are heated over a flame or in a heating mantle.
compatibility-measuring-only = A { $lower } is not heated: it is for measuring volume; heat would spoil its marks and may crack the glass.
compatibility-flame-only = A { $lower } is not put on a hob: it is heated in the flame of a lab burner or spirit lamp (on a tripod with a pipe-clay triangle), or in a muffle furnace.
compatibility-jacket = A { $lower } is not put on a hob or over a flame: its air gap keeps the heat out. Its contents are heated from inside — with an immersion heater.
compatibility-heater-too-wide = The immersion heater (≈ { $heater } mm wide) does not fit through the opening of the { $lower } (≈ { $opening } mm).
compatibility-electrodes-too-wide = Two electrodes (≈ { $need } mm needed) do not fit into the opening of the { $lower } (≈ { $opening } mm).
